{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"g-boot","type":"group","x":-400,"y":-420,"width":2220,"height":580,"color":"2","label":"Boot & Connection — [[03 Boot & Connection]]"},
		{"id":"g-lobby","type":"group","x":2240,"y":-420,"width":1080,"height":580,"color":"3","label":"Lobby & Profiles — [[04 Lobby & Profiles]]"},
		{"id":"g-join","type":"group","x":3420,"y":-420,"width":1080,"height":580,"color":"4","label":"Joining the World — [[05 Joining the World]]"},
		{"id":"g-move","type":"group","x":3420,"y":240,"width":1080,"height":560,"color":"5","label":"Movement & Position Sync — [[06 Movement & Position Sync]]"},
		{"id":"g-terrain","type":"group","x":3420,"y":880,"width":1080,"height":560,"color":"5","label":"Terrain & World Streaming — [[07 Terrain & World Streaming]]"},
		{"id":"g-enemy","type":"group","x":4540,"y":240,"width":1080,"height":560,"color":"5","label":"Enemies & AI — [[08 Enemies & AI]]"},
		{"id":"g-combat","type":"group","x":4540,"y":880,"width":1080,"height":560,"color":"5","label":"Combat & Damage — [[09 Combat & Damage]]"},
		{"id":"g-inv","type":"group","x":3980,"y":1520,"width":1080,"height":560,"color":"5","label":"Inventory, Items & Enchantments — [[10 Inventory, Items & Enchantments]]"},
		{"id":"g-end","type":"group","x":3980,"y":2160,"width":1080,"height":460,"color":"1","label":"Disconnect & Teardown — [[13 Disconnect & Teardown]]"},
		{"id":"g-camera","type":"group","x":3420,"y":-1050,"width":1080,"height":410,"color":"6","label":"Camera & Presentation — [[11 Camera & Presentation]] (side system)"},
		{"id":"g-admin","type":"group","x":5660,"y":240,"width":560,"height":560,"color":"6","label":"Admin & Debug — [[12 Admin & Debug]] (side system)"},
		{"id":"join-reducer","type":"text","text":"**join_world = one row move** — delete `LoggedOutPlayer`, insert `LoggedInPlayer` carrying `username`/`is_admin`/`profile_id`; `try_scaffold_profile` lazily creates `PlayerData`, 24-slot `PlayerInventory` (starter loadout), `PlayerStats`, `PlayerPosition`/`PlayerChunk` at origin. Client optimistically swaps waves: `SubscribeGame` in, lobby out. (join-1–3)","x":3480,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"join-file-methods","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/player/methods.rs","x":3480,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"join-spawn","type":"text","text":"**Entities spawn from rows** — the `LocalPlayerBinder` row fires `OnLocalPlayerInsert`: spawns `local_player.tscn` + `bullet_manager.tscn` (deferred). AOI `nearby_*` views spawn one `RemotePlayer` / `Enemy` / `Drop` puppet per row, skipping your own row via `DatabaseConnector.IsLocal`. (join-4–5)","x":4040,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"join-file-spawner","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Spawning/EntitySpawnerComponent.cs","x":4040,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-05","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/05 Joining the World.md","x":3760,"y":40,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"camera","type":"text","text":"**One camera rig, two presenters** — `CameraRigComponent` owns yaw/pitch/distance; the 2D presenter writes the player's phantom camera (priority 60 beats the lobby's), `World3DComponent` renders a cosmetic 3D SubViewport layer + Knight model (never a second simulation). Server hard-codes `CAMERA_VIEW_RADIUS` = 240 for enemy sim ranges. (camera-1–7)","x":4040,"y":-900,"width":400,"height":220},
		{"id":"camera-file","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Camera/CameraRigComponent.cs","x":4040,"y":-980,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"doc-11","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/11 Camera & Presentation.md","x":3480,"y":-900,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"lobby-ui","type":"text","text":"**Character select** — `CharSlotsPressed` loads `main.tscn`; `LobbyComponent.ShowLobby` shows the UI and raises the menu phantom camera to priority 60. A binder replays every profile row → one `profile_panel.tscn` each, with Join/Delete closures. CREATE calls `CreateProfile(name, \"Knight\")`. (lobby-1–4)","x":2300,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"lobby-file","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Lobby/LobbyComponent.cs","x":2300,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"lobby-server","type":"text","text":"**Profile reducers** — `create_profile` / `delete_profile` guard on `require_in_lobby`, validate name (1–20 chars, ≤3 profiles, no dupes), insert the row or run `teardown_profile` + delete. Caller-scoped views `local_lobby_player` / `local_player_profiles` stream only your own rows back. (lobby-1, 5–6)","x":2860,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"lobby-file-reducers","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/player/reducers.rs","x":2860,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-04","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/04 Lobby & Profiles.md","x":2580,"y":40,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"end-exit","type":"text","text":"**Three exits, one shape** — `leave_world` (no client UI calls it today), combat death (full `teardown_profile` first), and `client_disconnected` all delete `LoggedInPlayer` and reinsert `LoggedOutPlayer`. Client side is driven by row deletes: `OnLocalPlayerDelete` despawns the player + bullet manager, re-shows the lobby, swaps the waves back. (end-1–3)","x":4040,"y":2220,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"end-ghost","type":"text","text":"**Ghost rows linger** — `PlayerPosition`/`PlayerChunk` outlive logout and disconnect; every consumer guards with a `logged_in_player` semijoin. Reconnect replays boot with the saved token and rejoin skips scaffolding — progress, even the ghost position, resumes. Only death or `delete_profile` fully tears down. (end-4–6)","x":4600,"y":2220,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"combat-fire","type":"text","text":"**Client detects hits** — `CombatComponent` fires per weapon `FireRate`: a purely visual tracer plus timed `HitZone`s fused to land as the tracer crosses. Faction check (`CheckOpposition`, bit flags) → `ProcessHit` → `Reducers.ReportEnemyHit(enemyId)`. Enemy bullets overlapping your hurtbox echo their `SequenceStepRef` back via `ReportHit`. (combat-1–4, 6)","x":4600,"y":940,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"combat-file","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Weapon/CombatComponent.cs","x":4600,"y":1220,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"combat-server","type":"text","text":"**Server decides damage** — `report_enemy_hit` → `deal_damage_to_enemy`: damage recomputed server-side from the weapon + Strength (no client number trusted); a kill despawns the archetype and awards XP. `report_hit` resolves the `SequenceStepRef` to step damage → `deal_damage_to_player`, mitigated by Defense. HP = 0 → death, see teardown. (combat-5, 7–8)","x":5160,"y":940,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"combat-file-server","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/combat/mod.rs","x":5160,"y":1220,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"admin","type":"text","text":"**Admin & debug (CLI-only)** — `claim_admin`: a single global admin slot that survives the lobby↔world row moves. `spacetime call` reducers: `change_stats`, `give_item`/`remove_item`, live upserts for textures/items/enchantments/enemy defs, `spawn_enemy`/`despawn_enemy` (the only source of `immortal`/`is_elite`), on-demand world regen. Client: `DebugOverlay` on P. Server: `toggle_debug` SQL mirror table. (admin-1–9)","x":5720,"y":300,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"admin-file","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/main/admin.rs","x":5720,"y":580,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-12","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/12 Admin & Debug.md","x":5720,"y":670,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"doc-13","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/13 Disconnect & Teardown.md","x":4320,"y":2480,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"enemy-loop","type":"text","text":"**Server simulates enemies on schedules** — 2 s `tick_enemy_spawn`: per `BiomeRegion`, audience-gated, capped at `max_enemies` → `spawn_enemy_archetype`. 100 ms `tick_enemy_behavior`: sim-range gate, phase cycles, attack steps fire `BulletPatternEvent` rows (event table — never persists), movement integrates one 0.1 s step and wraps. (enemy-1–6)","x":4600,"y":300,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"enemy-file","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/enemy/reducers.rs","x":4600,"y":580,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"enemy-client","type":"text","text":"**Client renders the bullet hell** — `NearbyEnemies` rows → `Enemy` puppets (interpolation + hp mirror). Every in-world client receives all `BulletPatternEvent`s; each puppet keeps only its own → `BulletSpawnerComponent` builds ring/curtain/volley/shotgun/explosion transforms, SplitMix64-seeded by `event_id` so all clients derive identical trajectories. (enemy-7–9)","x":5160,"y":300,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"enemy-file-client","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Bullets/BulletSpawnerComponent.cs","x":5160,"y":580,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-08","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/08 Enemies & AI.md","x":4880,"y":670,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"doc-09","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/09 Combat & Damage.md","x":4880,"y":1310,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"inv-ui","type":"text","text":"**Inventory round-trips through the server** — 24 typed slots in one `PlayerInventory` row; the UI never mutates local state: drag = `SwapSlots` (validated both directions), hotbar 1–4 = `UseItem` (heal/buff; buffs tick down on a 1 s schedule), sidebar = `ApplyEnchantment` / `RemoveEnchantment`. Every mutation converges on `recompute_stats` (flat/mult pipeline) → row update repaints. (equip-1–8)","x":4040,"y":1580,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"terrain-stream","type":"text","text":"**Terrain streams by AOI** — game-wave views `nearby_terrain_tiles` / `nearby_hex_decor` recompute per chunk crossing. `TerrainComponent` caches rows, collapses a crossing's burst into ≤1 rebuild per frame, culls wrap-aware around the camera, and batches wedges into pooled `TileComponent` MultiMesh layers. (terrain-6–8)","x":3480,"y":940,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"terrain-file","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Terrain/TerrainComponent.cs","x":3480,"y":1220,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"terrain-gen","type":"text","text":"**World generated at publish, not join** — weighted-Voronoi biomes → regions (enemy-spawn districts) → per-wedge ground/overlay passes with adjacency rules + per-hex decor, writing `TriangleTile`/`HexDecor` rows. `place_building` / `remove_building` exist as reducers, but nothing calls or subscribes them. (terrain-1–5, 9)","x":4040,"y":940,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"terrain-file-gen","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/world/terrain/mod.rs","x":4040,"y":1220,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-07","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/07 Terrain & World Streaming.md","x":3760,"y":1310,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"inv-file","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Inventory/InventoryComponent.cs","x":4040,"y":1860,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"move-tick","type":"text","text":"**Movement is client-authoritative** — `LocalPlayer._PhysicsProcess`: WASD rotated by camera yaw → `MoveAndSlide`. `PositionSyncComponent` calls `report_movement` at a fixed 10 Hz; the server wraps the position onto the torus, rewrites `PlayerPosition` every call, and `PlayerChunk` only on a chunk crossing. (move-1–3)","x":3480,"y":300,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"move-file-sync","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Movement/PositionSyncComponent.cs","x":3480,"y":580,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"move-remote","type":"text","text":"**Positions echo back** — your own via `local_player_position` (snap only on a >50-unit desync, never on a lap wrap); everyone else's via the AOI view `nearby_remote_players` (2 chunk rings around your `PlayerChunk`) → `RemotePlayer` → `InterpolationComponent` lerps wrap-aware (`TorusMath.NearestCandidate`), deliberately a fraction behind. (move-4–6)","x":4040,"y":300,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"move-file-interp","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Movement/InterpolationComponent.cs","x":4040,"y":580,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-06","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/06 Movement & Position Sync.md","x":3760,"y":670,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"inv-loot","type":"text","text":"**Loot is physical** — right-click drop: `drop_item` clears the slot → `LootDrop` row streams via `nearby_loot_drops` → `Drop` node (5 s pickup lock for the dropper). Walk into the `Area2D` → `pickup_drop` finds a legal slot, deletes the row, recomputes. (loot-1–3)","x":4600,"y":1580,"width":400,"height":260},
		{"id":"inv-file-loot","type":"file","file":"client/Scripts/Components/Interaction/PickupComponent.cs","x":4600,"y":1860,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"doc-10","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/10 Inventory, Items & Enchantments.md","x":4320,"y":1950,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"conn-handshake","type":"text","text":"**Handshake** — `OnConnected`: store `Identity`, `SaveToken`, hook the username mirror, emit `Connected`. Server `client_connected`: a new identity gets a `LoggedOutPlayer` row (lobby state) plus a default \"Knight\" `PlayerProfile`; a returning one is left alone. (conn-1–2)","x":780,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"conn-file-tables","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/player/tables.rs","x":780,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"conn-waves","type":"text","text":"**Subscription waves** — `TableSubscriber` (both-orders guard on `Connected`): **base wave** (`AllTextures`/`AllItems`/`AllEnchantments` catalogs) + **lobby wave** (`LocalLobbyPlayer`, `LocalPlayerProfiles`). The game wave deliberately waits for join. `TableBinderComponent`s re-emit server rows as Godot signals. (conn-3–5)","x":1340,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"conn-file-sub","type":"file","file":"client/sstdbsdk/TableSubscriber.cs","x":1340,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"boot-server","type":"text","text":"**Publish = world genesis** — the `init` reducer runs once: plants 3 scheduled-reducer rows (enemy behavior 100 ms, enemy spawn 2 s, consumable tick), seeds textures/items/enchantments/enemy templates/world defs, `internal_add_chunks` (6×6 chunk grid + `MapConfig` with torus lap vectors), `internal_generate_world_proc(\"Earth\", 0)`. (boot-4–6)","x":-190,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"boot-file-lifecycle","type":"file","file":"server/spacetimedb/src/main/lifecycle.rs","x":-190,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"boot-client","type":"text","text":"**App launch (client)** — `project.godot` autoloads `DatabaseConnector` before any scene exists; `_Ready` stashes the singleton and calls `Connect(host, dbName)` immediately (per-host token via `AuthToken.Init`). Main scene = `lobby_gui.tscn`; `_Process` pumps `Conn.FrameTick()` every frame. (boot-1–3)","x":-1160,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":240},
		{"id":"boot-file-db","type":"file","file":"client/sstdbsdk/DatabaseConnector.cs","x":-1160,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":70},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# End-to-end runtime flow\nCurated overview of the whole game: **boot → connect → lobby → join → in-world loop → teardown**. Steps and anchor ids follow [[00 End-to-End Timeline Flowchart]]; each group links its system doc. Camera and Admin/Debug are side systems, branched off the main flow.","x":-1160,"y":-780,"width":400,"height":180},
		{"id":"doc-03","type":"file","file":"docs/Technical Design Docs/Description/03 Boot & Connection.md","x":-190,"y":100,"width":400,"height":60}
	],
